# Nominative (CLDR wide/stand-alone form): Unicode CLDR 47, locale eo,
# gregorian wide weekday names (cldr-dates-full/main/eo/ca-gregorian.json).
# Accusative -n: en.wiktionary.org "lundo" -- marks a SINGLE, specific
# occurrence when bare ("La stevardino flugos al Parizo lundon" -- the
# flight attendant will fly to Paris [this coming] Monday); under a
# distributive "ĉiu"/"ĉiun" (marker_every.voc) the SAME accusative is the
# attested "every ACCUSATIVE" recurrence idiom instead ("ĉiun lundon" --
# every Monday), exactly as it governs a counted unit ("ĉiun tagon").  The
# ADVERBIAL -e form ("lunde" -- on Mondays) is a deliberately different
# vocabulary slot, never folded in here, and gains no recurrence reading
# from "ĉiu" either -- see test_eo_weekday_case.py.
lundo
lundon
